,"order":7,"title":"Faithfulness Is the Standard","visual":{"takeaways":[{"text":"Righteousness is both a gift and a growing harvest"},{"text":"Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity"},{"text":"Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable"},{"text":"Build systems across all five pillars"}],"centralModel":"The one-talent servant fell for zero growth, not for having less."},"template":"summary","narration":"The master gave talents unevenly but expected equal faithfulness. The one-talent servant was condemned for zero growth, not for having less. Righteousness is both a gift and a harvest. Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity. Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable. Wisdom must follow power. Build systems across all five pillars.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"fade","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[],"durationSeconds":24,"generatedAdditions":[]}],"subject":"Riches","themeId":"mvp-default","audience":{"ageBand":"adult-beginner","difficulty":"intermediate","priorKnowledge":[]},"lessonId":"01a0cadc-f79e-798c-8f27-169a3d5b7505","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","objectiveIds":["01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991","01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105","01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01","01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606","01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c","01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6"],"schemaVersion":"1.8","targetDurationSeconds":180},"objectives":{"set":{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7668-ac5b-3ad7214dee32","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","status":"approved","promptId":"objectives","revision":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:31:45.136Z","vocabulary":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7c13-bb07-eab21dc97fec","term":"Positional Righteousness","order":1,"definition":"Righteousness received as a gift by grace through faith, a fixed legal credit that cannot be increased or diminished.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7c3b-8fff-e8bf58489812","term":"Harvest of Righteousness","order":2,"definition":"The dynamic, visible fruits and works of righteousness before people, which can and should be multiplied.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-74c5-9ae4-546c3def9a80","term":"Tzedakah","order":3,"definition":"The Hebrew word (T-Z-E-D-A-K-A-H) that treats morality, justice, and charity as inseparable parts of one whole.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7b57-993b-9e7083931f37","term":"Sowing Sparingly","order":4,"definition":"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love; a state of the giver's heart, not just an amount.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7307-bed2-070ed13cbed2","term":"Gleanings","order":5,"definition":"The corners and unharvested produce left in fields for the poor, the widow, and the stranger as a built-in safety net.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7814-978e-867ca029f928","term":"Steward","order":6,"definition":"A manager of God's property rather than an independent owner; in the Kingdom economy, owners are treated as rebels.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7962-a88d-8adfac2c73d7","term":"Budget","order":7,"definition":"A written plan for your money before it arrives.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-722e-972d-091a5973ef23","term":"50/30/20 Rule","order":8,"definition":"An allocation formula: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and investment, with savings growing as income grows.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7088-afb9-7104cb79125d","term":"Emergency Fund","order":9,"definition":"A liquid reserve of 3 to 6 months of living expenses that prevents breaking long-term investments in a crisis.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3","dbdda288-96d0-79a1-acf2-e6a27600477d"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"f9ed18f5-bfbf-78af-a209-208907dfac30","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7f9c-8613-7c9401997d28","term":"Risk Tolerance","order":10,"definition":"The level of investment risk a person can handle, which must be understood by investing in knowledge before investing money.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]}],"generatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","keyConcepts":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-792b-9cc4-1eba45825ab0","text":"Two manifestations of righteousness: gift (positional) versus harvest (practical)","order":1,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020","d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7dfc-8c1d-2e9182171a59","text":"Generosity as a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance","order":2,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7070-bdc1-3db31f7bd64b","text":"Tzedakah unites personal morality, justice, and charity into one whole","order":3,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7d99-a747-72bd5f757dd9","text":"Kingdom Economics laws: fairness over legal rights, debt cancellation, gleanings, prompt wages, refusing exploitation","order":4,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309","b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7a13-aa84-81fd72f59dee","text":"Power produces the miracle; wisdom sustains it","order":5,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7d6a-8534-12f9bcbfc19c","text":"Stewardship: God gives the power to get wealth and demands accountability","order":6,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf","49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7675-ad05-0967e85dd6d7","text":"Five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting/tracking, protection, savings, investment, debt management","order":7,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"f9ed18f5-bfbf-78af-a209-208907dfac30","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"9a6de675-995a-7740-ab5b-26f425655e0a","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"5d29fd16-f27e-7798-bd4a-a3c77b40545d","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]}],"modelCallId":"01a0cace-ecd7-75ef-acbe-73f2938e990f","ownerUserId":"01a0c938-7551-7405-a9e1-4db43e6bc491","promptVersion":"v2","idempotencyKey":"objectives.generate:01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92:objectives:01a0cacd-ada1-7d9c-b0a0-a25de9158d02:9c4bbd04d94cf9242ae2fa11ad3e8f7172f9445b507c65be9e9c2eef9128f09a:v2:8f2105d5dbadbcee68ef2dea5479e58606a6c9f025b1b65a221886e52910dc10:babdb06f58469cec7fe80bf7fb7f8d8dc91e47ca117caf46ace5c25ce955af75","misconceptions":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7a3f-95a0-02667ad6a12f","order":1,"correction":"The gift of righteousness is fixed, but the harvest of righteousness must be multiplied; works do not qualify us before God but demonstrate faith before people.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"a34c7386-4622-7b06-9259-8ceace8dbdb8","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Because righteousness is a gift, works are unnecessary."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7414-bc14-fdfe11435709","order":2,"correction":"Sowing sparingly describes the state of the giver's heart-reluctant compulsion or exhaustion-not merely the financial quantity.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Sowing sparingly is only about giving a small amount of money."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7a77-9f26-520c65153de3","order":3,"correction":"In the Hebrew scriptures, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have power to give violates Tzedakah.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-76b1-842a-bd56ed30ecef","order":4,"correction":"Power and wisdom are distinct yet both necessary; without wisdom to organize and structure, a person will burn out and destroy what was built-power produces the miracle, wisdom sustains it.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Having the power of God is enough to sustain a blessed life."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7e96-bf79-a3055dab3fec","order":5,"correction":"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; if you cannot manage 200,000 naira, 20 million will only enable more expensive mistakes.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"A bigger amount of money will solve money problems."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7801-8f13-476d334665f3","order":6,"correction":"Inflation and bank maintenance fees and levies slowly deplete idle capital; investment requires first investing in knowledge and understanding risk.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Leaving money in a bank account is a safe investment strategy."}],"sourceSnapshotId":"01a0cacd-ada1-7d9c-b0a0-a25de9158d02","assessmentQuestions":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-714b-809f-d23e7d4857c9","order":1,"question":"In your own words, what is the difference between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness?","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7677-b76f-a9e0300175f2","order":2,"question":"Name the three ramifications of Tzedakah and give one everyday example of each.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7ff2-bb12-ef0f010f7916","order":3,"question":"Choose two Kingdom Economics laws from the sermon and explain how each one protects poor or vulnerable people.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7113-9985-99c6a1a954c3","order":4,"question":"After Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, why did He command that she be given something to eat, and what does this teach about money management?","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7b43-89a5-da73a5c1c879","order":5,"question":"If your monthly income is 100,000 naira, use the 50/30/20 rule to calculate how much should go to needs, wants, and savings/investment.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-71d3-b7dc-6755f130b1d4","order":6,"question":"Why was the one-talent servant condemned even though he did not lose the money?","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]}],"configurationVersion":1,"prerequisiteKnowledge":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7dde-93f9-c630e3749e5f","text":"Basic familiarity with the Biblical narrative of David and Goliath and the roles of Goliath and King Saul","order":1,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"a34c7386-4622-7b06-9259-8ceace8dbdb8","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7335-a474-ed6de56a31ac","text":"Awareness that the sermons draw on specific scriptures such as Proverbs 8:18, 2 Corinthians 9, and Acts 20:32","order":2,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["1259c33f-c13b-733f-a31b-eac5bd884c63"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"8b3a2fbf-ae3e-7b3b-9c8e-2dfb5570438f","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["56a5c45d-a5ef-700a-a272-89b5569a62ea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"50ab6b8a-cab7-76cd-8432-fb39f839dbed","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7898-bb66-15571a6f6b14","text":"General understanding of money terms used in the sermons such as income, expenses, debt, savings, and interest","order":3,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a