6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6","verb":"compare","order":6,"setId":"01a0cace-ecd7-7668-ac5b-3ad7214dee32","revision":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","generated":true,"projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","statement":"Compare the outcomes of the servants in the Parable of the Talents and explain why the one-talent servant was condemned.","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","confidence":0.88,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"ownerUserId":"01a0c938-7551-7405-a9e1-4db43e6bc491"}]},"storyboard":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-798c-8f27-169a3d5b7505","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","title":"Sermon:Giving","scenes":[{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7747-8e44-ae7329d88b84","order":1,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7747-8e44-ae7329d88b84","order":1,"title":"One Word, Three Meanings","visual":{"prompt":"Meet the Hebrew idea of Tzedakah","question":"What if righteousness, justice, and generosity were one word?","supportingElements":["Righteous?","Just?","Generous?"]},"template":"hook","narration":"What if one word meant righteousness, justice, and generosity at the same time? Would it change how you see your faith and your money? Let's explore the Hebrew idea of Tzedakah.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"fade","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"subject","assetId":"01a0cae0-9426-7e70-b7ca-5400d108cf8c","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":12,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"hook","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-7747-8e44-ae7329d88b84","durationSeconds":12,"assetRequirements":[{"slot":"subject","purpose":"Evocative opening visual of an open Hebrew scroll suggesting the word Tzedakah"}],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-7383-a318-2557197f2f88"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-729a-8129-bfaf48faeb59","order":2,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-729a-8129-bfaf48faeb59","order":2,"title":"Two Kinds of Righteousness","visual":{"differences":["Gift: received by grace through faith","Gift: fixed legal credit, never changes","Harvest: grows and multiplies","Harvest: visible works before people"],"leftSubject":{"label":"Righteousness as a Gift"},"rightSubject":{"label":"Harvest of Righteousness"},"similarities":["Both must be active in a believer's life"]},"template":"comparison","narration":"Every believer has two kinds of righteousness. The first is a gift received by grace through faith. It is a fixed legal credit that never changes. The second is a harvest that can grow and multiply. This harvest shows up as visible works before people. Ignoring either kind creates a dangerous doctrinal imbalance.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020","d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"right-subject-image","assetId":"01a0cae4-f700-7f19-9adb-200f31c3caeb","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"illustration","slot":"left-subject-image","assetId":"01a0cae4-cf10-78b7-8a79-e25f2dde797e","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":19,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"comparison","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-729a-8129-bfaf48faeb59","durationSeconds":19,"assetRequirements":[],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-7e9a-bb7f-098de0027bc7"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7354-95cb-9e0b6787e590","order":3,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7354-95cb-9e0b6787e590","order":3,"title":"Tzedakah","visual":{"term":"Tzedakah","definition":"One Hebrew word uniting morality, justice, and charity as inseparable duties.","exampleText":"Refusing to give when you can violates Tzedakah.","exampleLabel":"Withholding help"},"template":"definition","narration":"The Hebrew word Tzedakah holds three inseparable meanings. First is personal morality, which means refusing to lie or steal. Second is justice, which means acting uprightly in business and legal dealings. Third is charity, which means giving to the poor as a matter of justice. Withholding help when you can give violates Tzedakah. These three must work together in daily conduct.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"visual-example","assetId":"01a0cae0-b4b7-7c4b-b8c0-d6037f2b7ae2","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":23,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"definition","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-7354-95cb-9e0b6787e590","durationSeconds":23,"assetRequirements":[{"slot":"visual-example","purpose":"Triptych illustration of the three meanings: honest character, fair dealing, giving to the poor"}],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-7aca-a6a2-9b0d7cfb4d30"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7dba-8053-24768f2d1aca","order":4,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7dba-8053-24768f2d1aca","order":4,"title":"Kingdom Economics in Action","visual":{"steps":["Return a poor debtor's cloak before sundown","Cancel debts every seven years (Jubilee)","Leave field-edge gleanings for the poor","Pay workers promptly","Never exploit desperation for profit"]},"template":"process","narration":"Kingdom Economics puts fairness above legal rights. If you take a poor debtor's cloak, return it before sundown. Every seven years, debts were canceled in the Jubilee. Landowners left gleanings at field edges for the poor and stranger. This built a safety net directly into profit-making. Workers must be paid promptly, not made to wait. Never exploit someone's desperation for profit. God judges those who oppress the afflicted.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309","b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"icon","slot":"step-5-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-7228-716c-a380-c8c38e3d4fd0","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-4-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-4e1c-78aa-8b7a-73a06b5ed4ed","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-3-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-2872-7ad1-8d13-b55b6e7ed106","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-2-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-03bf-7a65-8f7e-51267476fdd0","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-1-icon","assetId":"01a0cadf-d363-725e-8931-78ad3bb235cf","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":28,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"process","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-7dba-8053-24768f2d1aca","durationSeconds":28,"assetRequirements":[{"slot":"step-1-icon","purpose":"Icon of a cloak being returned at sunset"},{"slot":"step-2-icon","purpose":"Icon of a debt scroll being canceled"},{"slot":"step-3-icon","purpose":"Icon of a field with unharvested corners"},{"slot":"step-4-icon","purpose":"Icon of timely wages paid to a worker"},{"slot":"step-5-icon","purpose":"Icon of a balanced scale rejecting exploitation"}],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-77a7-82ee-deb4e38a23d0"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7aae-a0b7-c95171972638","order":5,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7aae-a0b7-c95171972638","order":5,"title":"Power Produces, Wisdom Sustains","visual":{"mappings":[{"analogy":"Power parted the sea","concept":"Moses' miracles"},{"analogy":"Wisdom stopped burnout","concept":"Jethro's delegation"},{"analogy":"Power gave life","concept":"Raising Jairus's daughter"},{"analogy":"Wisdom kept her alive","concept":"Commanding she be fed"}],"sourceConcept":"God's power vs. God's wisdom","familiarSystem":"Miracle then maintenance"},"template":"analogy","narration":"Moses had miraculous power but was burning out. Jethro taught him structural delegation to survive. Power produces the miracle, but wisdom sustains it. Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, then commanded she be fed. Without wisdom, the miracle would have been lost. Apply this to money: power earns it, wisdom keeps it.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea","afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"central-visual","assetId":"01a0cae0-d61b-7b3e-9ce8-017ad7eb2831","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":20,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"analogy","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-7aae-a0b7-c95171972638","durationSeconds":20,"assetRequirements":[{"slot":"central-visual","purpose":"Illustration pairing a dramatic miracle with a quiet act of practical care"}],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-7735-895b-c23e1b09c7b5"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7314-8fb8-ec7b7b8fa0d7","order":6,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7314-8fb8-ec7b7b8fa0d7","order":6,"title":"Five Pillars and the 50/30/20 Rule","visual":{"kind":"asset","shape":"system","labels":[{"id":"lbl-budgeting","text":"Budgeting","anchor":"top-left"},{"id":"lbl-protection","text":"Protection","anchor":"top-right"},{"id":"lbl-savings","text":"Savings","anchor":"left"},{"id":"lbl-investment","text":"Investment","anchor":"right"},{"id":"lbl-debt","text":"Debt management","anchor":"bottom"}],"baseAssetSlot":"diagram"},"template":"labelled-diagram","narration":"There are five pillars of financial stewardship. They are budgeting, protection, savings, investment, and debt management. Use the 50/30/20 rule to allocate your income. Fifty percent goes to needs like rent and food. Thirty percent goes to wants like dining out. Twenty percent goes to savings and investment. If you earn 100,000 naira, save 20,000 first.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":["50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings & investment","Earn 100,000 naira? Save 20,000 first."],"assetBindings":[{"role":"diagram","slot":"diagram","assetId":"211b6fd2-19e2-7eef-bf16-b89db79c6a67"}],"durationSeconds":22,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"labelled-diagram","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-7314-8fb8-ec7b7b8fa0d7","durationSeconds":22,"assetRequirements":[],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-76e3-80b2-9c4b3c99d909"]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-76a9-a2bc-1f81bf3e8af1","order":7,"scene":{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-76a9-a2bc-1f81bf3e8af1","order":7,"title":"Faithfulness Is the Standard","visual":{"takeaways":[{"text":"Righteousness is both a gift and a growing harvest"},{"text":"Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity"},{"text":"Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable"},{"text":"Build systems across all five pillars"}],"centralModel":"The one-talent servant fell for zero growth, not for having less."},"template":"summary","narration":"The master gave talents unevenly but expected equal faithfulness. The one-talent servant was condemned for zero growth, not for having less. Righteousness is both a gift and a harvest. Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity. Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable. Wisdom must follow power. Build systems across all five pillars.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"fade","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[],"durationSeconds":24,"generatedAdditions":[]},"template":"summary","stableSceneId":"01a0cadc-f79e-76a9-a2bc-1f81bf3e8af1","durationSeconds":24,"assetRequirements":[],"narrationBlockIds":["01a0cad9-e117-7f09-8dd0-2c0d46511cf4"]}],"status":"draft","subject":"Riches","promptId":"storyboard","revision":14,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T20:44:34.078Z","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","contentHash":"3ca55dca42c618a12a97869164b0941aa4370ffede282ab8a2e282948231854b","generatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:44:34.078Z","modelCallId":"01a0cadc-f79e-784c-9572-ae6af21d45fb","objectiveIds":["01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991","01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105","01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01","01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606","01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c","01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6"],"outlineSetId":"01a0cad5-389d-7228-9f90-d037d4f13282","promptVersion":"v2","schemaVersion":1,"configurationVersion":1,"totalDurationSeconds":148,"basedOnNarrationSetId":"01a0cad9-e117-78bd-8a12-b19453113c26","outlineSetContentHash":"0a90daf0a9e81ba5d9d2e6c4588524163234be101ac032749819552648dfc606","targetDurationSeconds":180,"narrationSetContentHash":"47e754ac0c08e1cb6c3f1d5394b7cb3721701498a828ddf03910817b9b2c82e3"},"configuration":{"id":"01a0cace-9e5b-7f80-86b8-274275f067e1","tone":"friendly","ageBand":"adult-beginner","subject":"Riches","version":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T20:28:53.723Z","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:28:53.723Z","difficulty":"intermediate","lessonTitle":"Sermon:Giving","ownerUserId":"01a0c938-7551-7405-a9e1-4db43e6bc491","visualTheme":"mvp-default","videoApproach":"standard","creativeStylePack":"editorial","targetDurationSeconds":180,"includeRecallQuestions":false,"sourceParsedDocumentVersion":94508325},"schemaVersion":"lesson-version-v1","creativeDesign":null,"sourceSnapshot":{"id":"01a0cacd-ada1-7d9c-b0a0-a25de9158d02","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"C   E   L   E   B   R   A   T   I   O   N       C   H   U   R   C   H       I   N   T   E   R   N   A   T   I   O   N   A   L","order":1,"blockId":"0477caa3-79bc-74a3-baec-2505f71439d5","pageEnd":1,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":1,"sectionId":"b2cc0b51-4574-78a2-b034-3ebce99d7ae0"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"SERMON SERIES TRANSCRIPTS &amp; STUDY GUIDE","order":1,"blockId":"694b5bef-deda-75ae-9334-ddbd71655474","pageEnd":1,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":1,"sectionId":"6254d1cb-ab02-7e38-9ce3-e52d7e3b71ce"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Featuring the Apostolic Teachings on Kingdom Generosity and Financial Stewardship Delivered during August 2026 services","order":2,"blockId":"31beb41f-1828-7326-93af-e63d5b019cea","pageEnd":1,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":1,"sectionId":"6254d1cb-ab02-7e38-9ce3-e52d7e3b71ce"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In the month of August 2026, Celebration Church International held a life-transforming teaching series centered around  spiritual  consecration,  spiritual  authority,  and  financial  principles.  This  document  compiles  and structures  the  transcripts  and  theological  frameworks  of  two  crucial  teachings  from  the  series:  the  Sunday Service on August 30th, 2026, titled 'Durable Riches & Righteousness' ,  and the Midweek Service on August 26th, 2026, titled 'Managing Personal Resources' .","order":1,"blockId":"89f268e8-a1c2-73ba-bc57-67d0cb7bc211","pageEnd":2,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":2,"sectionId":"93483be8-d678-70af-bbce-ea1f309cb876"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"These sermons, delivered under apostolic oversight, seek to balance faith-based new-creation realities with solid, practical systems of wisdom. In 'Durable Riches & Righteousness' ,  the congregation was instructed on the twin manifestations of righteousness (righteousness as a gift versus the harvest of righteousness) and the deep-seated  systems  of  justice  and  charity  embedded  in  Biblical  economic  law.  In 'Managing  Personal Resources' ,  the  focus  shifted  to  financial  stewardship  and  the  practical  habits-such  as  budgeting, tracking, protection,  saving,  and  responsible  debt  management-necessary  to  sustain  divine  blessings.  This  guide serves as an authoritative reference and study companion.","order":2,"blockId":"8671642c-0e48-7b7c-ac4f-74359d56063e","pageEnd":2,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":2,"sectionId":"93483be8-d678-70af-bbce-ea1f309cb876"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"How you know you can beat Goliath depends on who is asking. If it is Goliath, you stand on the covenant: 'You dare defy the armies of the living God?' But if it is King Saul who asks, you point to physical evidence: 'I have killed a lion and a bear.' Before God, we present only faith and Christ's finished work; before people, there must be a visible harvest of works to show.","order":1,"blockId":"c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"a34c7386-4622-7b06-9259-8ceace8dbdb8"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Date: August 30th, 2026 | Service: 1st Service | Preacher: Lead Pastor","order":1,"blockId":"2fc030fd-5eb9-70a6-8241-af6fa2a4175a","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"83ce68bb-38b6-7020-90c5-2f50e412bad1"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Riches and honor are with me, enduring riches and righteousness. I traverse the way of righteousness in the midst of the paths of justice, that I may cause those who love me to inherit wealth, that I may fill their treasuries.","order":1,"blockId":"1259c33f-c13b-733f-a31b-eac5bd884c63","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"8b3a2fbf-ae3e-7b3b-9c8e-2dfb5570438f"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A central theme of the teaching is that there are two distinct manifestations of righteousness in the life of every  believer,  and  both  must  be  visible  and  active.  Understanding  the  distinction  is  the  key  to  avoiding  a dangerous doctrinal imbalance.","order":1,"blockId":"c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In 2 Corinthians 9, the Apostle Paul uses agricultural metaphors to connect righteousness directly with financial generosity. True Christian generosity is not a forced contribution or a compliance gimmick, but a natural, willing overflow  of  spiritual  righteousness.  The  term 'sowing  sparingly' does  not  merely  describe  the  financial quantity, but rather the state of a giver's heart. Sowing sparingly means giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love. On the other hand, a bountiful sower is cheerful and content, operating out of divine contentment ( 'godliness with contentment is great gain' ), which allows them to give sacrificially and joyfully.","order":1,"blockId":"19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1. Righteousness as a Gift (Positional Righteousness): This is the legal foundation of our salvation. It is received entirely by grace through faith, apart from human works. As stated in Galatians 3:6 and Romans 4, 'Abraham believed God, and it was accounted to him for righteousness.' This is a fixed, perfect legal credit on the  believer's  account  that  cannot  be  added  to,  multiplied,  or  diminished.  It  is  a  gift  that  establishes  one's permanent relationship and covenant standing with God.","order":2,"blockId":"7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"2.  The  Harvest  of  Righteousness  (Practical  Righteousness): Based  on  2  Corinthians  9:10  ( 'He  who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your seed for sowing and increase the harvest of your righteousness' ), this manifestation is dynamic and agricultural. While the gift of righteousness cannot  increase,  the  harvest  of  righteousness  can  and  should  be  multiplied.  This  represents  the  visible demonstrations, fruits, and works of righteousness before men. As the preacher emphasized, 'It  is  true  that righteousness is not by works, but you cannot separate works from righteousness.' Works do not qualify us before God, but they demonstrate our faith before people.","order":3,"blockId":"d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826","pageEnd":3,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Kingdom Economics operates on laws that directly contradict the ruthless, self-serving capitalistic models of the world. Believers are called to implement these ancient structural consecrations in their business dealings and personal finances:","order":1,"blockId":"b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"To fully grasp the Biblical framework of righteousness, one must look past the language barrier and explore the original  Hebrew  word Tzedakah (spelled:  T-Z-E-D-A-K-A-H).  While  English  translations  often  split  this  into distinct concepts of morality, justice, or charity, the Hebrew mind understood them as inseparable parts of a single whole. Tzedakah has three critical ramifications:","order":1,"blockId":"06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"1. Personal Morality: This is the internal rectitude of the believer-standing clean before God, refusing to lie, steal, or compromise one's moral character.","order":2,"blockId":"74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba"},{"kind":"list","items":["Fairness Over Legal Rights (Deuteronomy 24:10-13): Biblical law dictates that if you take a poor debtor's cloak  as  collateral,  you  must  return  it  to  him  before  sundown  so  he  can  sleep.  Legal  right  must  never supersede basic humanity and fairness."],"order":2,"blockId":"23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"2. Justice: This is the structural expression of righteousness-refusing to oppress the vulnerable, standing up against unfairness, and acting uprightly in all societal, legal, and business transactions.","order":3,"blockId":"fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba"},{"kind":"list","items":["Periodic  Debt  Cancellation  (The  Jubilee): The  Old  Testament  instituted  a  cycle  where  debts  were canceled every seven years. God warned that lenders must not refuse to help a borrower on the sixth year simply because the year of cancellation was near."],"order":3,"blockId":"f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"list","items":["Leaving Gleanings for the Poor: Business owners in Israel were commanded not to harvest their fields to the  very  edges,  but  to  leave  the  corners  and  unharvested  produce  for  the  poor,  the  widow,  and  the stranger.  This  is  a  Biblical  business  model  that  builds  a  social  safety  net  directly  into  profit-generating activities."],"order":4,"blockId":"a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"3.  Charity  and  Generosity: In  the  Hebrew  scriptures,  giving  to  the  poor  is  not  categorized  as  'optional benevolence'; it is classified as a matter of justice and righteousness . To withhold help from the poor when you have the power to give is to violate Tzedakah .","order":4,"blockId":"49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba"},{"kind":"list","items":["Prompt Payment of Workers (Jeremiah 22:13, James 5:4): Withholding wages or paying employees late is  a  severe  violation  of  righteousness.  The  scripture  issues  a  woe  to  those  who  build  their  houses  by unrighteousness and use their neighbor's service without wages."],"order":5,"blockId":"9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"list","items":["Refusing  to  Exploit  Bargaining  Power: Believers  must  never  monetize  another  person's  desperation (e.g., buying an asset at a ridiculously low price because the owner is facing an emergency). Oppressing the afflicted or robbing the poor prompts the Lord to step in as a judge to plead their cause and plunder the soul of the plunderers (Proverbs 22:22-23)."],"order":6,"blockId":"b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","pageEnd":5,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The Prophetic Framework for Daily Conduct","order":1,"blockId":"16867493-f89b-7ed2-a06d-ca7981ce8b46","pageEnd":6,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":6,"sectionId":"194c9b12-5a0a-7a29-8d00-af9882f09b02"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"During the sermon, a notable miracle testimony was shared to demonstrate the reality of God's healing power. Sister Janet Augustine had been diagnosed with a painful fibroadenoma (breast lump) that had grown so severe she could not wear a bra for up to two hours without intense discomfort. Preparing for a scheduled surgical  removal,  she  fully  participated  in  the  20  days  of  prophetic  prayer  and  meditation.  On  the  final  day, during apostolic declarations for healing, she declared in faith: 'From today, this pain in my breast must stop.'","order":1,"blockId":"6f6f5d43-2866-796c-827b-bdcf292f6743","pageEnd":6,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":6,"sectionId":"101edc93-0f7b-74a1-8a73-ee173ad70c75"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The pain stopped immediately. Her subsequent medical checks revealed that the breast no longer ached, and the lump had dramatically shrunk back to its normal, healthy size. This testimony served as a catalyst of faith for the entire congregation, demonstrating that God continues to validate His Word with creative, extraordinary miracles.","order":2,"blockId":"f52f9977-81e5-7bbd-bcfb-80b24b9ab7cb","pageEnd":6,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":6,"sectionId":"101edc93-0f7b-74a1-8a73-ee173ad70c75"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"To build a strong spiritual posture and maintain character across the days of the week, the lead pastor guided the  congregation through a series of specific prophetic confessions. These declarations reinforce character, eradicate the fear of the future, and align the believer's steps with divine purpose:","order":2,"blockId":"fd4d9b67-4895-7944-8e1b-ba0364dc00d0","pageEnd":6,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":6,"sectionId":"194c9b12-5a0a-7a29-8d00-af9882f09b02"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Before diving into money management mechanics, the teaching establishes two foundational spiritual laws of stewardship:","order":1,"blockId":"aa10be8e-f777-7242-b70f-d7fccc397e24","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Date: August 26th, 2026 | Service: Midweek Service | Preacher: Teaching Pastor","order":1,"blockId":"5ac2d903-ce27-7d47-9e46-dfe033b0c700","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"fa419a84-c11c-7253-94dc-6f799706aa7e"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"And now, brethren, I commend you to God and to the word of His grace, which is able to build you up and give you an inheritance among all those who are sanctified.","order":1,"blockId":"56a5c45d-a5ef-700a-a272-89b5569a62ea","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"50ab6b8a-cab7-76cd-8432-fb39f839dbed"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The sermon begins with an illuminating  look  at Exodus 18:14-20 .  Moses,  having  performed  mind-boggling miracles-including  parting  the  Red  Sea  and  bringing  plagues  upon  Egypt-was  sitting  from  morning  until evening  judging  the  disputes  of  all  Israel.  His  father-in-law,  Jethro,  observed  this  and  delivered  a  startling critique: 'The thing that you do is not good. Both you and these people... will surely wear yourselves out, for this thing is too much for you.'","order":1,"blockId":"afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In  Mark  5:41-43,  after  Jesus  raised  Jairus's  daughter  from  the  dead-an  undeniable  demonstration  of creative,  supernatural  power-He  immediately  commanded  that 'something  should  be  given  her  to  eat.' Jesus recognized that while the power of God brought her back to life, the practical wisdom of nourishment was  required  to  keep  her  alive.  Without  wisdom  following  power,  she  would  have  died  again.  Similarly, believers must apply practical financial wisdom to sustain the financial blessings God brings their way.","order":1,"blockId":"2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Truth 1: God Gives the Resources: As stated in Deuteronomy 8:18, God does not give wealth directly; He gives 'the  power  to  get  wealth.' This  means  God  deposits  intellectual  capacity,  physical  skills,  career opportunities, and access to key relationships. All good and perfect gifts come from the Father of lights (James 1:17). Since all we have originates from Him, we are not independent owners; we are stewards. In the economy of the Kingdom, owners are treated as rebels; we are simply managers of God's property.","order":2,"blockId":"2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Jethro advised Moses to institute structural delegation and systems. This narrative establishes a major spiritual paradigm: the power of God is distinct from the wisdom of God , yet both are necessary. A person can have the power of God in raw, visible form, but without the wisdom of God to organize and structure their life, they will burn out and destroy what has been built. Power produces the miracle; wisdom sustains it.","order":2,"blockId":"44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Truth 2: God Demands Accountability: In  the  Parable of the Talents (Matthew 25), the master distributed resources unequally-giving five talents, two talents, and one talent based on individual ability. However, the master expected the exact same standard of faithfulness  and  interest from  everyone.  The  servant  with  one talent was not condemned because he made less than the five-talent servant; he was condemned as a 'wicked and  lazy  servant' because  he  made no interest and  showed  zero  growth.  Your  current  financial  level  is  a stewardship test: if you cannot manage 200,000 naira, receiving 20 million will not solve your problems-it will only enable you to make more expensive mistakes.","order":3,"blockId":"49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e","pageEnd":7,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The  teaching  structures  personal  finance  into  five  practical  pillars.  To  be  a  faithful  steward,  one  must systematically build and implement systems across each of these categories:","order":1,"blockId":"f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A budget is simply a written plan for your money before it arrives. Many believers fail because they budget only in their minds or fail to track where their money goes. As Jesus said in Luke 14:28, 'Which of you, intending to build a tower, does not sit down first and count the cost, whether he has enough to finish it?' Tracking means looking  through  bank  statements  and  eliminating  hidden  leaks-such  as  unused  subscriptions,  impulse spending on delicacies (like 'goat meat' or gourmet ice cream), and lifestyle inflation.","order":1,"blockId":"d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The biggest financial mistake is focusing solely on making money while ignoring the very real risk of losing it. Proverbs 23:5 warns that 'wealth sprouts wings and flies away like an eagle.' Unforeseen health or physical emergencies can instantly wipe out years of hard-earned savings. Protection means building defensive walls around your wealth: · Health  Insurance: An  absolute  necessity.  The  pastor  shared  how  health  insurance  fully  covered  his daughters'  prenatal,  delivery,  and  postnatal  care  at  zero  cost.  Conversely,  an  uninsured  child's  emergency neonatal treatment (jaundice) cost another family 4.6 million naira in unplanned expenses. · Motor Vehicle Insurance: Essential for protecting assets. Car insurance has shifted from 2.5% to 5% of the vehicle's value. It prepares you for the reckless driving of others. The pastor shared that a 1.44 million naira repair bill for a vehicle collision was fully paid by insurance, saving him from a massive financial shock. · Emergency Funds: A liquid reserve representing 3 to 6 months of living expenses. Having this fund prevents","order":1,"blockId":"19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"f9ed18f5-bfbf-78af-a209-208907dfac30"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Savings is capital set aside for future use. Proverbs 21:20 states: 'There is desirable treasure and oil in the dwelling of the wise, but a foolish man squanders it.' According to Proverbs 6:6-8, we must learn from the ant, which gathers her food in the harvest to prepare for winter. Savings is crucial because without accumulated capital, you will never be able to seize investment opportunities (e.g., buying a deeply discounted asset) when they present themselves.","order":1,"blockId":"7a32b18c-fe32-715f-b6f2-3ef07a0836cf","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"9a6de675-995a-7740-ab5b-26f425655e0a"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"you from having to break long-term investments whenever an emergency arises.","order":2,"blockId":"dbdda288-96d0-79a1-acf2-e6a27600477d","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"f9ed18f5-bfbf-78af-a209-208907dfac30"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"THE 50/30/20 BUDGET FORMULA The 50/30/20 Allocation Rule: A highly practical formula for financial discipline: · 50%  Needs: Non-negotiable  survival  costs:  Rent,  basic  feeding,  essential  transportation,  internet,  and protection. · 30% Wants: Desires that you can live without: Fine dining, fast food (shawarma/pizza), and luxury items. · 20% Savings & Investment: Funds reserved for future growth. As income grows, the percentage allocated to savings and investment must increase.","order":2,"blockId":"dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f","pageEnd":9,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A Lesson in Honor & Communication: In September 2021, a borrower collected 2 million naira from the teaching pastor to serve as proof of funds for travel. Due to a misunderstanding, the borrower assumed the funds were a gift, leaving the pastor's personal wedding savings depleted. Once the misunderstanding was cleared,  the  borrower  did  not  flee  or  hide.  Instead,  they  communicated  consistently  every  single  month, explaining their progress, and paid the debt back systematically, little by little. Honest communication and a rigorous plan preserve relationships and maintain honor.","order":1,"blockId":"3741dd17-412f-713a-b187-12fbc871e77e","pageEnd":11,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"9e3655e2-959d-7538-809f-dd3db79654d9"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Funding a personal lifestyle with debt is a direct path to financial ruin. As Proverbs 22:7 states, 'The rich rules over the poor, and the borrower is servant to the lender.' When you borrow, you enter a position of submission. Furthermore,  Psalm  37:21  declares  that 'the  wicked  borrow  and  never  repay.' If  you  are  in  debt,  you  must establish a clear, realistic payback plan and maintain open communication with your lender.","order":1,"blockId":"09df5ee4-b668-7289-9457-76279f00717b","pageEnd":11,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"5d29fd16-f27e-7798-bd4a-a3c77b40545d"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Investment is the act of allocating resources with the expectation of generating profit. Simply leaving money in a bank account is a poor strategy; inflation and bank maintenance fees/levies will slowly deplete your capital. However,  before  investing  money  in  stocks,  bonds,  mutual  funds,  or  real  estate,  you  must first  invest  in knowledge .  You  must  understand  your  risk  tolerance  and  risk  appetite.  Many  fall  victim  to  financial  scams because  they  chase  unreasonable  returns  (e.g.,  60%  payouts  or  food-stuff  gimmicks)  without  doing  due diligence.","order":1,"blockId":"66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60","pageEnd":11,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Use  the  following  diagnostic  matrix  to  evaluate  your  current  standing  across  the  five  pillars  and  create  a structured plan for spiritual and practical financial alignment:","order":1,"blockId":"d1ca8a64-9ed7-757e-b99f-62587d9beb97","pageEnd":11,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"a0a99f03-ea40-79ce-b52f-33877d79008e"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"We serve God by His Spirit. We boast in Christ Jesus. We put no confidence in the flesh. We experience progress and joy in the faith, reaching a billion souls in 10,000 cities-because we are Celebration Church! May the Lord multiply your seed sown and increase the harvest of your righteousness. Amen!","order":1,"blockId":"0fdcd24d-e0fa-7630-b6f5-74f456dfb6e0","pageEnd":12,"revision":0,"corrected":false,"pageStart":12,"sectionId":"9b12d846-7d1e-7aa6-b8bc-34bf2693420e"}],"tables":[{"rows":[["1. Introduction & Sermon Series Overview","Page 2"],["2. Sermon 1: Durable Riches &",""],["Righteousness","Page 3"],["3. Weekly Consecrations & Declarations","Page 5"],["4. Sermon 2: Managing Personal Resources","Page 6"],["5. Personal Financial Consecration Matrix","Page 8"]],"order":1,"columns":["Column 1","Column 2"],"pageEnd":2,"tableId":"7135cb02-01c9-769b-8eda-9fb0f946baf1","pageStart":2,"sectionId":"cbea4081-91ae-73eb-b025-b5fbc63c1cc1"},{"rows":[["Day","Daily Declaration & Confession Theme","Scriptural / Theological Focus"],["I walk in divine confidence. God made me and I am His. He chose me and He will continue to help me; therefore, I am not afraid of the future.","Identity & Fearlessness","Monday"],["I begin with favor. There is fire on my altar; my spirit is awake and my joy is renewed. Prophecies go ahead of me to direct my steps.","Spiritual Fervency","Tuesday"],["I am fruitful and productive. The Lord is with me, and His hand is upon the work of my hands. I flourish where planted; my labor is not in vain.","Fruitfulness & Productivity","Wednesday"],["My family and I are preserved from all evil. Our going out is safe, our coming in is blessed. We share and receive good news and testimonies.","Preservation & Protection","Thursday"],["My heart is open and receptive to the Lord. I discern His voice and obey it. I seek Him and find Him, sensitive to divine timing and aligned.","Divine Guidance & Discernment","Friday"],["I bask in the joy of my salvation. I remember how He saved me, washed me, forgave me, and covered me; and in this, I rejoice exceedingly.","Gratitude & Salvation","Saturday"],["I enter His gates with thanksgiving. I do not spectate; I participate and immerse myself. This is my season for encountering the Lord's power.","Honor & Sacred Service","Sunday"]],"order":2,"columns":["Column 1","Column 2","Column 3"],"pageEnd":6,"tableId":"3ea4a879-38a9-74ea-8518-08266fb9c6fc","pageStart":6,"sectionId":"194c9b12-5a0a-7a29-8d00-af9882f09b02"},{"rows":[["Pillar","Diagnostic Evaluation Questions Spiritual / Practical Action Step",""],["Do I have a written plan for every income before it arrives? Am I tracking small daily leaks?","Implement the 50/30/20 Rule using a physical ledger or digital tracking app. Check bank statements monthly.","1. Budgeting"],["Would a medical emergency or auto accident bankrupt me? Do I have an emergency fund?","Obtain a basic health insurance policy. Set aside a portion of income until 3-6 months of expenses are saved.","2. Protection"],["Am I squandering 100% of my income? Am I prepared for seasonal drops or dry seasons?","Automate a 10% to 20% savings sweep from your salary. Cultivate the wisdom of the ant (Proverbs 6:6-8).","3. Savings"],["Am I leaving my savings to deplete in standard accounts? Am I chasing high-yield scams?","Decline 'get-rich-quick' schemes. Commit to reading one book on financial markets before investing in assets.","4. Investment"],["Am I borrowing to fund my lifestyle? If I am currently in debt, do I have a proactive plan?","Eradicate consumer debt. If currently in debt, write down a repayment plan and send monthly updates to the lender.","5. Debt"]],"order":3,"columns":["Column 1","Column 2","Column 3"],"pageEnd":11,"tableId":"211b6fd2-19e2-7eef-bf16-b89db79c6a67","pageStart":11,"sectionId":"a0a99f03-ea40-79ce-b52f-33877d79008e"}],"figures":[],"sections":[{"level":1,"order":1,"heading":"Document","pageEnd":1,"blockIds":["0477caa3-79bc-74a3-baec-2505f71439d5"],"tableIds":[],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":1,"sectionId":"b2cc0b51-4574-78a2-b034-3ebce99d7ae0","reviewOrder":null},{"level":1,"order":2,"heading":"THE HARVEST OF RIGHTEOUSNESS","pageEnd":2,"blockIds":["694b5bef-deda-75ae-9334-ddbd71655474","31beb41f-1828-7326-93af-e63d5b019cea"],"tableIds":[],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":1,"sectionId":"6254d1cb-ab02-7e38-9ce3-e52d7e3b71ce","reviewOrder":null},{"level":1,"order":3,"heading":"TABLE OF CONTENTS","pageEnd":2,"blockIds":[],"tableIds":["7135cb02-01c9-769b-8eda-9fb0f946baf1"],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":2,"sectionId":"cbea4081-91ae-73eb-b025-b5fbc63c1cc1","reviewOrder":null},{"level":1,"order":4,"heading":"SERMON SERIES OVERVIEW & INTRODUCTION","pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["89f268e8-a1c2-73ba-bc57-67d0cb7bc211","8671642c-0e48-7b7c-ac4f-74359d56063e"],"tableIds":[],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":2,"sectionId":"93483be8-d678-70af-bbce-ea1f309cb876","reviewOrder":null},{"level":1,"order":5,"heading":"1. SERMON 1: DURABLE RICHES & RIGHTEOUSNESS","pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["2fc030fd-5eb9-70a6-8241-af6fa2a4175a"],"tableIds":[],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"83ce68bb-38b6-7020-90c5-2f50e412bad1","reviewOrder":null},{"level":1,"order":6,"heading":"ANCHOR SCRIPTURE: PROVERBS 8:18, 20-21","pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["1259c33f-c13b-733f-a31b-eac5bd884c63"],"tableIds":[],"figureIds":[],"pageStart":3,"section