gs. Third is charity, which means giving to the poor as a matter of justice. Withholding help when you can give violates Tzedakah. These three must work together in daily conduct.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"visual-example","assetId":"01a0cae0-b4b7-7c4b-b8c0-d6037f2b7ae2","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":23,"generatedAdditions":[]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7dba-8053-24768f2d1aca","order":4,"title":"Kingdom Economics in Action","visual":{"steps":["Return a poor debtor's cloak before sundown","Cancel debts every seven years (Jubilee)","Leave field-edge gleanings for the poor","Pay workers promptly","Never exploit desperation for profit"]},"template":"process","narration":"Kingdom Economics puts fairness above legal rights. If you take a poor debtor's cloak, return it before sundown. Every seven years, debts were canceled in the Jubilee. Landowners left gleanings at field edges for the poor and stranger. This built a safety net directly into profit-making. Workers must be paid promptly, not made to wait. Never exploit someone's desperation for profit. God judges those who oppress the afflicted.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","b29eff38-6707-7ec8-9cc2-3acf8b734309","b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"icon","slot":"step-5-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-7228-716c-a380-c8c38e3d4fd0","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-4-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-4e1c-78aa-8b7a-73a06b5ed4ed","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-3-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-2872-7ad1-8d13-b55b6e7ed106","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-2-icon","assetId":"01a0cae0-03bf-7a65-8f7e-51267476fdd0","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"},{"role":"icon","slot":"step-1-icon","assetId":"01a0cadf-d363-725e-8931-78ad3bb235cf","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":28,"generatedAdditions":[]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7aae-a0b7-c95171972638","order":5,"title":"Power Produces, Wisdom Sustains","visual":{"mappings":[{"analogy":"Power parted the sea","concept":"Moses' miracles"},{"analogy":"Wisdom stopped burnout","concept":"Jethro's delegation"},{"analogy":"Power gave life","concept":"Raising Jairus's daughter"},{"analogy":"Wisdom kept her alive","concept":"Commanding she be fed"}],"sourceConcept":"God's power vs. God's wisdom","familiarSystem":"Miracle then maintenance"},"template":"analogy","narration":"Moses had miraculous power but was burning out. Jethro taught him structural delegation to survive. Power produces the miracle, but wisdom sustains it. Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, then commanded she be fed. Without wisdom, the miracle would have been lost. Apply this to money: power earns it, wisdom keeps it.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea","afe140a5-8141-7709-8e11-8dfb41acef12"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[{"role":"illustration","slot":"central-visual","assetId":"01a0cae0-d61b-7b3e-9ce8-017ad7eb2831","provenance":"ai_generated","visualRole":"decorative"}],"durationSeconds":20,"generatedAdditions":[]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-7314-8fb8-ec7b7b8fa0d7","order":6,"title":"Five Pillars and the 50/30/20 Rule","visual":{"kind":"asset","shape":"system","labels":[{"id":"lbl-budgeting","text":"Budgeting","anchor":"top-left"},{"id":"lbl-protection","text":"Protection","anchor":"top-right"},{"id":"lbl-savings","text":"Savings","anchor":"left"},{"id":"lbl-investment","text":"Investment","anchor":"right"},{"id":"lbl-debt","text":"Debt management","anchor":"bottom"}],"baseAssetSlot":"diagram"},"template":"labelled-diagram","narration":"There are five pillars of financial stewardship. They are budgeting, protection, savings, investment, and debt management. Use the 50/30/20 rule to allocate your income. Fifty percent goes to needs like rent and food. Thirty percent goes to wants like dining out. Twenty percent goes to savings and investment. If you earn 100,000 naira, save 20,000 first.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"cut","onScreenText":["50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings & investment","Earn 100,000 naira? Save 20,000 first."],"assetBindings":[{"role":"diagram","slot":"diagram","assetId":"211b6fd2-19e2-7eef-bf16-b89db79c6a67"}],"durationSeconds":22,"generatedAdditions":[]},{"id":"01a0cadc-f79e-76a9-a2bc-1f81bf3e8af1","order":7,"title":"Faithfulness Is the Standard","visual":{"takeaways":[{"text":"Righteousness is both a gift and a growing harvest"},{"text":"Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity"},{"text":"Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable"},{"text":"Build systems across all five pillars"}],"centralModel":"The one-talent servant fell for zero growth, not for having less."},"template":"summary","narration":"The master gave talents unevenly but expected equal faithfulness. The one-talent servant was condemned for zero growth, not for having less. Righteousness is both a gift and a harvest. Tzedakah demands integrity, justice, and generosity. Kingdom Economics protects the vulnerable. Wisdom must follow power. Build systems across all five pillars.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["f95b27d2-c234-738f-87ee-cf404117fd5a"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"05d93e71-77f1-79af-903f-44645f4eca12","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"transition":"fade","onScreenText":[],"assetBindings":[],"durationSeconds":24,"generatedAdditions":[]}],"subject":"Riches","themeId":"mvp-default","audience":{"ageBand":"adult-beginner","difficulty":"intermediate","priorKnowledge":[]},"lessonId":"01a0cadc-f79e-798c-8f27-169a3d5b7505","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","objectiveIds":["01a0cace-ecd7-7355-b1db-e3dafa507991","01a0cace-ecd7-7970-8683-661a513bb105","01a0cace-ecd7-7b8d-9e03-abc39630db01","01a0cace-ecd7-7a1a-9412-52d954644606","01a0cace-ecd7-7239-afef-9a0413bb4e1c","01a0cace-ecd7-7bc6-ae8b-1812d9d98dc6"],"schemaVersion":"1.8","targetDurationSeconds":180},"objectives":{"set":{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7668-ac5b-3ad7214dee32","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","status":"approved","promptId":"objectives","revision":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","projectId":"01a0cacc-4547-7835-b7c4-fcd924b96a92","updatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:31:45.136Z","vocabulary":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7c13-bb07-eab21dc97fec","term":"Positional Righteousness","order":1,"definition":"Righteousness received as a gift by grace through faith, a fixed legal credit that cannot be increased or diminished.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7c3b-8fff-e8bf58489812","term":"Harvest of Righteousness","order":2,"definition":"The dynamic, visible fruits and works of righteousness before people, which can and should be multiplied.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-74c5-9ae4-546c3def9a80","term":"Tzedakah","order":3,"definition":"The Hebrew word (T-Z-E-D-A-K-A-H) that treats morality, justice, and charity as inseparable parts of one whole.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7b57-993b-9e7083931f37","term":"Sowing Sparingly","order":4,"definition":"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love; a state of the giver's heart, not just an amount.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7307-bed2-070ed13cbed2","term":"Gleanings","order":5,"definition":"The corners and unharvested produce left in fields for the poor, the widow, and the stranger as a built-in safety net.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7814-978e-867ca029f928","term":"Steward","order":6,"definition":"A manager of God's property rather than an independent owner; in the Kingdom economy, owners are treated as rebels.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2e7f2eb1-2d9f-71fc-863c-14b5cea9acaf"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7962-a88d-8adfac2c73d7","term":"Budget","order":7,"definition":"A written plan for your money before it arrives.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["d8d10398-fc31-7207-8067-7d205b09e480"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-722e-972d-091a5973ef23","term":"50/30/20 Rule","order":8,"definition":"An allocation formula: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and investment, with savings growing as income grows.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7088-afb9-7104cb79125d","term":"Emergency Fund","order":9,"definition":"A liquid reserve of 3 to 6 months of living expenses that prevents breaking long-term investments in a crisis.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["19c878fa-239b-717b-b639-679449af7ad3","dbdda288-96d0-79a1-acf2-e6a27600477d"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"f9ed18f5-bfbf-78af-a209-208907dfac30","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7f9c-8613-7c9401997d28","term":"Risk Tolerance","order":10,"definition":"The level of investment risk a person can handle, which must be understood by investing in knowledge before investing money.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]}],"generatedAt":"2026-09-22T20:29:13.815Z","keyConcepts":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-792b-9cc4-1eba45825ab0","text":"Two manifestations of righteousness: gift (positional) versus harvest (practical)","order":1,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","c963b0b0-1108-7ea7-940d-01123d9cc020","d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7dfc-8c1d-2e9182171a59","text":"Generosity as a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance","order":2,"sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7070-bdc1-3db31f7bd64b","text":"Tzedakah unites personal morality, justice, and charity into one whole","order":3,"source