righteousness must be multiplied; works do not qualify us before God but demonstrate faith before people.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["c2a2b9c1-12af-73f2-84f0-432fe91a4b6a"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"a34c7386-4622-7b06-9259-8ceace8dbdb8","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Because righteousness is a gift, works are unnecessary."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7414-bc14-fdfe11435709","order":2,"correction":"Sowing sparingly describes the state of the giver's heart-reluctant compulsion or exhaustion-not merely the financial quantity.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["19d141cb-9c20-7966-8416-afe5863ec966"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"945ac743-1f71-77fb-a524-2fe425066f93","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Sowing sparingly is only about giving a small amount of money."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7a77-9f26-520c65153de3","order":3,"correction":"In the Hebrew scriptures, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have power to give violates Tzedakah.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-76b1-842a-bd56ed30ecef","order":4,"correction":"Power and wisdom are distinct yet both necessary; without wisdom to organize and structure, a person will burn out and destroy what was built-power produces the miracle, wisdom sustains it.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["44fdb66c-c888-7231-9e57-293f33c4efea"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"1ec7b67c-4e37-70cc-8c39-afaab46897f4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325},{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Having the power of God is enough to sustain a blessed life."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7e96-bf79-a3055dab3fec","order":5,"correction":"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; if you cannot manage 200,000 naira, 20 million will only enable more expensive mistakes.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["49ec6ab8-4041-757d-8594-ceb5170b4b8e"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"62712383-7b98-77d3-875f-babdb7c3ef46","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"A bigger amount of money will solve money problems."},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7801-8f13-476d334665f3","order":6,"correction":"Inflation and bank maintenance fees and levies slowly deplete idle capital; investment requires first investing in knowledge and understanding risk.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":11,"blockIds":["66e311a8-add0-7a1d-8ef6-093444c88a60"],"pageStart":11,"sectionId":"db102ffa-82bb-745f-be36-1708b4b455c4","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}],"misconception":"Leaving money in a bank account is a safe investment strategy."}],"sourceSnapshotId":"01a0cacd-ada1-7d9c-b0a0-a25de9158d02","assessmentQuestions":[{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-714b-809f-d23e7d4857c9","order":1,"question":"In your own words, what is the difference between righteousness as a gift and the harvest of righteousness?","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":3,"blockIds":["7af22950-46db-75ef-a410-7afe128a90aa","d0c0e6db-3dc0-7132-80b1-b30a86bfb826"],"pageStart":3,"sectionId":"ae281305-b489-7168-892d-1b43eb1f6932","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7677-b76f-a9e0300175f2","order":2,"question":"Name the three ramifications of Tzedakah and give one everyday example of each.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["06034497-9561-73ab-9a48-7e0b4dd07526","49c29e8f-988b-7974-8e1c-98507766b8dc","74a62c36-c225-74cd-ab8b-4c70bfa21c0c","fe3027da-43fa-7c54-abee-645434318ebe"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"b8b1cd0e-0c38-7a4c-b81c-f5b63a2e5bba","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7ff2-bb12-ef0f010f7916","order":3,"question":"Choose two Kingdom Economics laws from the sermon and explain how each one protects poor or vulnerable people.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":5,"blockIds":["23d224bd-1662-7e5a-93b1-c26aa4216531","9192540a-67d8-7cd6-8b2a-7c756cd244d9","a8294542-be65-7173-89e6-421f1913a466","b2b17cf5-d046-7435-b026-b9e3ddb02152","f1f0308a-70b9-7c61-bf74-93a6bf2ad067"],"pageStart":5,"sectionId":"0b36c7d7-5424-7634-928c-baea7fb3aa2b","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7113-9985-99c6a1a954c3","order":4,"question":"After Jesus raised Jairus's daughter, why did He command that she be given something to eat, and what does this teach about money management?","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":7,"blockIds":["2f2a6065-ab09-75d0-b83d-f382b614cf54"],"pageStart":7,"sectionId":"27a1c852-016a-7f51-86c4-bea4e36155a1","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-7b43-89a5-da73a5c1c879","order":5,"question":"If your monthly income is 100,000 naira, use the 50/30/20 rule to calculate how much should go to needs, wants, and savings/investment.","sourceRefs":[{"pageEnd":9,"blockIds":["dd8e865f-a031-7bdc-8f60-67cddffe293f"],"pageStart":9,"sectionId":"b9aeaa29-20f7-7aed-9afc-8d6e97474ef2","documentId":"147dae4b-e3d7-7b84-8397-e1bf5d641a5c","parsedDocumentVersion":94508325}]},{"id":"01a0cace-ecd7-71d3-b7dc-6755f13